      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the USB_A connector J4 has D+ (pin 3) labeled NET0013 and D- (pin 2) labeled NET0017, while on the SkylabModule sheet the SKW92A U11 has USB- (pin 19) labeled NET0013 and USB+ (pin 18) labeled NET0017.",
      "expected": "USB D+ must connect to the module's USB+ pin and D- to USB-, so the two data lines are not crossed.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J4 USB_A: pin 3 (D+) -> NET0013, pin 2 (D-) -> NET0017 (EthernetAndPower sheet)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U11 SKW92A: pin 19 (USB-) -> NET0013, pin 18 (USB+) -> NET0017 (SkylabModule sheet)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The USB data pair is polarity-swapped, so USB data communication with the SKW92A will not work (USB power is unaffected).",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains at least one clear connectivity deviation: the BBQ10KBD keyboard matrix has column 5 and row 3 shorted together on net NET0018, which would break matrix scanning. A second likely deviation is that the USB D+/D- pair appears crossed between connector J4 and the SKW92A USB pins."
}

